[size=4][i]Tattoos that change the body and hair wearing them.[/i][/size]

[size=5][b]Description[/b][/size]

This patch connects [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/180775]Magic Tattoos Framework[/url] (MTF) to [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/19080]RaceMenu[/url]. A tattoo tier can make the actor bigger or smaller, reshape their body with BodySlide sliders, or recolor their hair while it shows, for example a muscular build on a warrior's mark, or frost-white hair on a frost mage's sigil.

It adds a [b]RaceMenu[/b] plugin to MTF's menu and to [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/196803]Magic Tattoos UI[/url]. RaceMenu itself is not changed.

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/180775]Magic Tattoos Framework[/url] 0.7.0 or later, and its requirements
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/19080]RaceMenu[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/13048]PapyrusUtil SE[/url]
[*]For Body shape: a body with BodySlide morphs, such as [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/30174]CBBE 3BA[/url], built in BodySlide with [b]Build Morphs[/b] checked. Outfits need morphs built too, or the body grows through them.
[*]Optional: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/196803]Magic Tattoos Framework - SKSE UI[/url], an editor in the SKSE Menu Framework menu, with live previews. It makes setting up tiers with these effects far easier.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]

Install with your mod manager and enable [font=Courier New]MTF_Plugin_RaceMenu.esp[/font]. It is ESL-flagged and only lists [font=Courier New]Skyrim.esm[/font] and [font=Courier New]MagicTattoosFramework.esp[/font] as masters, so it can go anywhere after MTF. RaceMenu is found at runtime; if it isn't loaded, the plugin stays unregistered and does nothing.

[size=5][b]Effects[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Actor scale[/b] ([i]while shown[/i]): the actor is 50 to 200% of their usual size
[*][b]Body shape[/b] ([i]while shown[/i]): the body takes one of 23 shapes at 5 to 100% strength
[*][b]Hair color[/b] ([i]while shown[/i]): the hair, and optionally the brows and beard, are tinted any color
[/list]

Every effect has a [b]Transition[/b] setting, 0 to 30 seconds (5 by default). The body or hair eases from how it looks now to the new look over that time instead of changing at once, starting and stopping gently, and eases back the same way when the tier stops. 0 changes it instantly. A change that arrives mid-transition carries on from wherever it is. Loading a save finishes any transition that was under way.

[b]Actor scale[/b] scales RaceMenu's root [font=Courier New]NPC[/font] node, so it multiplies with RaceMenu's own height slider. Several tiers multiply together.

[b]Body shape[/b] moves CBBE 3BA BodySlide sliders through RaceMenu's body morphs. It adds to the body's own preset, including one from OBody, rather than replacing it, so the same strength changes any body by the same amount. At 100% strength, each shape adds this much to its sliders; lower strengths scale them down:

[list]
[*][b]Muscular[/b]: [font=Courier New]MuscleAbs[/font], [font=Courier New]MuscleArms[/font], [font=Courier New]MuscleBack_v2[/font], [font=Courier New]MuscleButt[/font], [font=Courier New]MuscleLegs[/font], [font=Courier New]MusclePecs[/font] +100; [font=Courier New]MuscleMoreAbs_v2[/font], [font=Courier New]MuscleMoreArms_v2[/font], [font=Courier New]MuscleMoreLegs_v2[/font] +50
[*][b]Bigger bust[/b]: [font=Courier New]Breasts[/font] +100
[*][b]Smaller bust[/b]: [font=Courier New]BreastsSmall[/font] +100
[*][b]Perkier bust[/b]: [font=Courier New]BreastPerkiness[/font] +100, [font=Courier New]PushUp[/font] +50
[*][b]Saggier bust[/b]: [font=Courier New]BreastGravity2[/font] +100
[*][b]Perkier nipples[/b]: [font=Courier New]NipplePerkiness[/font] +100, [font=Courier New]NippleLength[/font] +50
[*][b]Bigger butt[/b]: [font=Courier New]Butt[/font] +100, [font=Courier New]BigButt[/font] +50
[*][b]Smaller butt[/b]: [font=Courier New]ButtSmall[/font] +100
[*][b]Rounder butt[/b]: [font=Courier New]RoundAss[/font] +100, [font=Courier New]AppleCheeks[/font] +50
[*][b]Wider hips[/b]: [font=Courier New]Hips[/font] +100, [font=Courier New]HipUpperWidth[/font] +50
[*][b]Narrower hips[/b]: [font=Courier New]HipNarrow_v2[/font] +100
[*][b]Thicker thighs[/b]: [font=Courier New]Thighs[/font] +100, [font=Courier New]ThighFBThicc_v2[/font] and [font=Courier New]ThighOutsideThicc_v2[/font] +50
[*][b]Thinner thighs[/b]: [font=Courier New]SlimThighs[/font] +100, [font=Courier New]LegsThin[/font] +50
[*][b]Slender[/b]: [font=Courier New]SlimThighs[/font] +100, [font=Courier New]LegsThin[/font] and [font=Courier New]ButtNarrow_v2[/font] +50
[*][b]Chubby[/b]: [font=Courier New]ChubbyArms[/font], [font=Courier New]ChubbyButt[/font], [font=Courier New]ChubbyLegs[/font], [font=Courier New]ChubbyWaist[/font] +100; [font=Courier New]BigBelly[/font] +50
[*][b]Pregnant[/b]: [font=Courier New]PregnancyBelly[/font] +100
[*][b]Older[/b]: [font=Courier New]BreastGravity2[/font], [font=Courier New]ButtSaggy_v2[/font] +100; [font=Courier New]ButtUnderFold[/font] +50
[*][b]Younger[/b]: [font=Courier New]BreastPerkiness[/font] +100, [font=Courier New]NipplePerkiness[/font] +50
[*][b]Longer schlong[/b]: [font=Courier New]Length[/font], [font=Courier New]SOS - SchlongLength[/font] +100
[*][b]Thicker schlong[/b]: [font=Courier New]Thickness[/font], [font=Courier New]SOS - SchlongGirth[/font] +100
[*][b]Larger glans[/b]: [font=Courier New]Head[/font], [font=Courier New]SOS - GlansSize[/font] +100
[*][b]Larger balls[/b]: [font=Courier New]SOS - BallsSize[/font] +100 (futanari addon only)
[*][b]Smaller balls[/b]: [font=Courier New]SOS - BallsSmall[/font] +100 (futanari addon only)
[/list]

Older and Younger only change the body. RaceMenu can't reshape a face from a script, so for an aged face, pair Older with an MTF face tattoo carrying a wrinkle texture.

Shrinking uses the bodies' own shrink sliders ([font=Courier New]BreastsSmall[/font], [font=Courier New]ButtSmall[/font], [font=Courier New]HipNarrow_v2[/font], [font=Courier New]SlimThighs[/font], [font=Courier New]SOS - BallsSmall[/font]) rather than taking away from the size sliders, which would push past the flat shape on a small preset. TNG and the futanari addon have no shrink sliders for length, girth or the glans, so those shapes only grow.

Several Body shape tiers combine: different shapes stack, so Muscular and Pregnant together give both. Two tiers that move the same slider don't add up; that slider takes the strongest value either asks for. Opposites such as Bigger and Smaller bust move different sliders, so they partly cancel.

Bodies without these sliders don't change. That includes the vanilla male body and BHUNP, which uses different slider names.

The schlong, glans and balls shapes move the genital meshes from [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/104215]TNG[/url], which RaceMenu morphs alongside the body. Each mesh only responds to its own slider names:

[list]
[*]TNG's male meshes (the [font=Courier New][TNG][/font] slider sets) use [font=Courier New]Length[/font], [font=Courier New]Thickness[/font] and [font=Courier New]Head[/font]. They have no balls slider.
[*]The ERF Futanari addon uses the old SOS names, such as [font=Courier New]SOS - SchlongLength[/font].
[/list]

Either kind needs to be built in BodySlide with [b]Build Morphs[/b] checked. You'll see [font=Courier New].tri[/font] files next to the meshes, for example [font=Courier New]actors/character/character assets/TNG/m_genitals.tri[/font].

[b]Hair color[/b] sets the tint that Skyrim's hair shader multiplies the hair texture by, the same tint RaceMenu's hair color slider changes. [b]Covers[/b] picks the hair alone, or the hair, brows and beard together. When several Hair color tiers show at once, the one that started last wins, and when it stops the next one takes over. When none are left, the hair goes back to its own color.

Because the tint multiplies the texture, it can darken a color or shift it, but not lighten it. Hair with pale, neutral textures, which is most hair made to be recolored in RaceMenu, takes any color well. Dark or already-colored hair textures only get darker or tinted, so a platinum color on black hair stays dark.

Wigs from [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/31300]KS Hairdos SMP[/url] (KS Wigs SMP) change too, along with the hair under them. Other wigs worn as armor may not: a script can't list the parts of a wig, so the plugin looks for the part names KS uses, based on the wig's mesh file.

A new hairstyle or wig picks up the color within a couple of seconds, and so does a wig taken off and put back on, or hair whose physics reset.

All three effects work on the player and NPCs. RaceMenu saves them with the game, so they stay after a load until the tier stops.

[size=5][b]Resetting[/b][/size]

If a body, size or hair change ever stays after its tattoo is gone, you can undo everything the plugin has changed. Open the console and enter:

[code]setpqv MTF_Plugin_RaceMenu ResetOnLoad 1[/code]

Then save and load that save. Every actor the plugin has changed goes back to their own shape, size and hair color, and the Papyrus log shows [font=Courier New][MTF_Plugin_RaceMenu] reset N actor(s)[/font]. The setting turns itself off again, so later loads don't reset. Skyrim's console can't run a script directly, which is why it waits for a load.

The reset only touches this plugin's own changes. RaceMenu sliders, OBody presets and other mods' morphs stay as they were. A tier that is still showing comes back the next time it starts.

[size=5][b]Uninstalling[/b][/size]

Take off any tattoo whose tiers use these effects, so the body and hair go back to normal, or use the reset above. Then save, quit, and disable the plugin.

[size=5][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/size]

The Papyrus log ([font=Courier New]Documents/My Games/Skyrim Special Edition/Logs/Script/Papyrus.0.log[/font]) should show [font=Courier New][MTF_Main] Registered 'proteux-mtf.racemenu'[/font] a few seconds after loading a save. If it doesn't, check that RaceMenu and MTF are enabled and that [font=Courier New]MTF_Plugin_RaceMenu.esp[/font] loads after [font=Courier New]MagicTattoosFramework.esp[/font].

Each Body shape change logs a line such as [font=Courier New][MTF_Plugin_RaceMenu] body morphs on Lydia: Breasts=1.000000[/font] once it finishes (after the transition), so you can tell whether the effect ran. If the line appears but the body doesn't change, the body has no morphs. Rebuild it in BodySlide with [b]Build Morphs[/b] checked; a [font=Courier New]femalebody.tri[/font] file should appear next to [font=Courier New]femalebody_0.nif[/font] and [font=Courier New]femalebody_1.nif[/font].

Each Hair color change logs a line such as [font=Courier New][MTF_Plugin_RaceMenu] hair color on Lydia: HairFemaleNord06=#C0392B[/font] once it finishes, listing each hair, brow and beard part it tinted ([font=Courier New]none[/font] when the hair goes back to its own color). If the line lists parts but the hair doesn't change, that hair's texture is too dark to show the tint, or it's a wig the plugin can't find parts for.

Each time a Hair color tier starts, the log also lists what the effect can see, in lines starting [font=Courier New][MTF_Plugin_RaceMenu] hair debug:[/font]: the actor's head parts, anything worn in the hair slots (31 and 41) with the part names its mesh suggests, and the parts being tinted. Each part shows [font=Courier New](no node)[/font] if the actor doesn't have it, or its color right now.

[url=https://github.com/proteux/skyrim-magic-tattoo-connectors/blob/main/connectors/racemenu/TESTING.md]TESTING.md[/url] walks through checking each effect in game.

